    "teacher_markdown": "Expected observations (not a single fixed answer, since this is open tinkering): \r\n- Starting at 2 means only two passes print (steps 2 and 3).\r\n- Changing the condition to steps < 2 means only two passes print as well (steps 0 and 1) — a good moment to notice that changing either the start value or the condition changes how many times the loop runs, even though they’re different parts of the loop."
